-- title:
--   Orders unchanged in a separable constant-field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $k$, $k'$, $F$, $F'$ be fields equipped with algebra structures $k \to k'$, $k \to F$, $F \to F'$, $k' \to F'$ and $k \to F'$, compatibly in the sense that $k \to k' \to F'$ and $k \to F \to F'$ are scalar towers, and assume $k'$ is algebraic and separable over $k$. Assume moreover that $F'$ is generated over $F$ by the constants, i.e. the $F$-subalgebra of $F'$ generated by the image of $k'$ is all of $F'$. Let $x$ be a place of $F$ over $k$ and $x'$ a place of $F'$ over $k'$, where a place of $F$ over $k$ consists of a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $k$, distinct from $F$ itself, and whose underlying ring is a principal ideal ring. Assume $x$ and $x'$ are compatible in the sense that the preimage of the valuation subring of $x'$ under $F \to F'$ is exactly the valuation subring of $x$. Then for every $f \in F$ one has $\operatorname{ord}_{x'}(\text{image of } f \text{ in } F') = \operatorname{ord}_x(f)$, where $\operatorname{ord}$ denotes minus the logarithm of the associated height-one-spectrum adic valuation, i.e. the normalised integer-valued order function of the discrete valuation ring.
--
--   This is the statement that a constant-field extension generated by a separable algebraic extension of the constant field is unramified at every place, so that orders of functions already in $F$ may be computed indifferently at $x$ or at $x'$. It is used to transport order computations between a function field and its base change along a separable extension of constants, and is cited in the comparison of orders under constant extensions and in the analysis of the Hasse invariant at supersingular points on modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_ord_algebraMap_eq_ord_of_comap_eq_of_isSeparable_of_adjoin_eq_top.lean

